WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.900
Yugi Muto assembled the Millennium Puzzle 
and became the guardian of the Shadow Games.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.260
Pegasus has a Millennium Item 
of his own - the Millennium Eye.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.800
Yugi accepts Pegasus's challenge 
and goes to Duelist Kingdom.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.940
Pegasus stole his grandfather Sugoroku's 
soul, and Yugi intends to rescue him.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.940
He battles alongside his trusted 
friends and with his other self.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:44.300
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.210
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.960
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.660
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.760
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.130
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:20.060
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.310
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:33.580
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.320
What is truly precious?

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:49.570
Clash!  Blue-Eyes vs Red-Eyes

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:03.040
Seto Kaiba is heading towards my island?

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.680
Don't worry.  We'll take care of him.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.340
We'll make sure Kaiba never 
reaches Duelist Kingdom.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.980
No!  Stay away from Seto Kaiba.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:25.840
Our contract takes effect when I defeat 
Yugi boy, so there should be no problems.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.980
Then Kaiba Corporation will be ours.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:42.340
We'll not only get Kaiba Corporation's cutting 
edge technology, but also Seto Kaiba's knowledge.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:52.340
Seto Kaiba, I look forward to meeting you.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.500
Yugi battled impressively.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:13.700
The card I drew was Exodia the Forbidden One.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.250
The fires of rage!  Exodo Flame!

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.880
No matter how strong your cards, they're 
meaningless if they have no heart.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.820
Miracles happen when your 
heart and cards become one.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.060
I want to battle him again.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:43.570
But first, there's someone I must 
defeat using this Duel Disk System.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:53.860
Big brother!

00:03:54.380 --> 00:04:02.890
The person who plotted with traitors and 
kidnapped Mokuba to gain control of Kaiba Corporation.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.100
Pegasus J. Crawford.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:11.600
I will defeat you with my own hands!

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.800
What is it, Bakura?

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.560
Look at this.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.540
The Millennium Ring's spike is 
pointing towards Pegasus's castle.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.700
You're right.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:47.380
The day I transferred 
to Domino High School...

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:54.370
He's joining our class today.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.840
How's that!

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.000
Yugi, it's your turn.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:05.220
It reacted to your Millennium Puzzle.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:13.440
Your Millennium Ring is reacting 
to Pegasus's Millennium Item?

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.660
Millennium Item?

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:20.800
Maybe the Millennium Ring 
detects Millennium Items.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:28.660
I don't know what the Millennium 
Items are or where they came from.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:40.820
So my Millennium Puzzle isn't 
the only Millennium Item.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:55.140
Since the day I solved the Millennium 
Puzzle, another version of myself lives within me.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.580
I want to solve this mystery.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:04.680
If I solve this mystery, I may be able 
to free my Grandpa from the Shadow Realm.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:07.620
Just wait, Grandpa.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.220
What's going on?

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:31.760
Who's flying a helicopter 
in the middle of the night?

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.300
What's happening?

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.420
Kaiba!

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.660
It's been awhile, Yugi.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.600
Oh yeah.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.800
Here's your deck, Kaiba.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.870
I kept it for you.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.310
I guess I should thank you.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.540
Kaiba, did you learn about 
the heart of the cards?

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:20.020
What is it?

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:23.410
I don't have an answer yet.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:32.920
To save Mokuba and Kaiba Corporation, 
I'll do anything to defeat Pegasus.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:34.430
Kaiba...

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:41.470
Wait, Kaiba!

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:48.480
In Duelist Kingdom, everyone is fighting hard to 
achieve their dreams by collecting ten Star Chips.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:51.060
So that they can battle against Pegasus.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:56.420
I don't know your situation, but you 
can't cut ahead of everyone in line!

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:04.720
Jonouchi!

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.640
Are you okay, Jonouchi?

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.300
Damn!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:13.600
Jonouchi, I can't believe you're actually 
able to participate in this tournament.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.360
Be quiet!

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.640
I had the skills to make the quarterfinals!

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.540
Of the local tournament.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:26.920
If you qualified as a duelist, 
this must be a lame tournament.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.120
What?

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.060
Don't do it, Jonouchi!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:40.870
Wait, Kaiba!  I'm no longer 
a weak duelist like before!

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:47.700
It's true, Kaiba.  Jonouchi defeated 
Mai Kujaku and Dinosaur Ryuzaki.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:55.980
Let's duel!  If you want to duel 
Pegasus, then defeat me first!

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.680
Don't do it!

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.080
Yeah.  You'll pop a blood vessel.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.440
What's wrong, Kaiba?

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.820
Battle me right here!

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.940
Interesting.

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:10.730
I'll destroy your fake 
and fragile confidence.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.400
Kaiba!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.800
Don't worry.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:18.420
We won't play for Star Chips.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:25.120
Jonouchi will help me test 
my new Duel Disk System.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:28.210
A new Duel Disk System?

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.920
Wear that on your left arm.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.200
What is this?

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.820
It's a Duel Disk.

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:48.480
It's a new card battle 
machine that I invented.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:53.540
This system allows for virtual 
simulation duels without a Duel Ring.

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:57.700
First, equip the deck 
holder on your left arm.

00:09:57.980 --> 00:09:59.800
Then what?

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:01.110
Watch.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:07.460
Place your deck in the holder.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:15.490
Your draw your card from the deck holder 
and play it by placing it on the Duel Disk.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:20.730
Then you throw the Duel Disk on to the field.

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:22.420
Here I go!

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:27.940
Battle Ox!

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:38.620
The Duel Disk's Hyper 3-D Engine quickly processes the 
card's visual data and transforms it into Solid Vision.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:46.420
That's incredible!  Kaiba has taken 
card battling to a whole new level!

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:10.420
How interesting.  I'll take 
you on with this card!

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.150
Battle!

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.340
Here I go!

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:22.420
Go, Armored Lizard!

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:28.660
Battle Ox, slice your enemy!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.000
Good!  It managed to survive!

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:38.980
You fool.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:40.580
Go!

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.620
My card...

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:53.250
When your monster is destroyed, 
retrieve your Duel Disk.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:58.420
I'll pass my turn until 
you play another monster.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.640
He's treating me like a beginner.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.070
Just you watch!

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.620
Here I go!

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:14.180
Flame Swordsman!

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:17.580
It has more attack points than your monster!

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.760
Flaming Battle Sword!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:23.860
No!  Battle Ox is strong 
against Fire Attribute!

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.420
Its powerful axe destroys 
your Flame Swordsman.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:35.540
I knew you were the weakest 
duelist in history.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:42.660
I place Polymerization and Mystic 
Horseman on my Duel Disk.

00:12:56.700 --> 00:13:00.660
You won't make a fool out of me!  Here I go!

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:05.060
Swamp Battleguard!

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.940
Axe Raider!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.740
Battle Steer!

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.000
Garoozis!

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.460
Rock Ogre Grotto #1!

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:23.220
Rude Kaiser...

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:36.640
What happened to your momentum, Jonouchi?

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.160
Are you done already?

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.360
It's no good.  I can't win.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:42.800
He's much more skilled than me.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.500
Stop acting pathetic!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:47.280
Stand up, Jonouchi!

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:48.170
Jonouchi!

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:52.180
That's right!  I don't 
want to see you like this!

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:54.350
Be quiet!

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:58.400
Listen up!  I'm not giving up!

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.600
The battle is just getting started.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:04.820
Face my Red-Eyes B. Dragon!

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.720
Jonouchi!

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.500
It's his trump card!

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.000
Here I go!

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.640
Black Fireball!

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:22.270
All right!

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:26.000
Winning one battle is hardly 
a reason to celebrate.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:29.920
That proves you're the 
weakest duelist in history.

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:30.960
What?

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:36.500
My deck contains a card 
that your friend retrieved.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.460
Come out, Blue-Eyes!

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:52.580
Prepare yourself!  Burst 
Stream of Destruction!

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:05.860
Damn!

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:08.420
Jonouchi!

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.320
Jonouchi.

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:16.080
Our battle showed you how 
terrifying dueling can be.

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:20.100
I don't know how an amateur 
like you kept winning.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:25.440
Jonouchi, you look good 
on your hands and knees.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.880
You can't even stand up, you loser.

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:30.240
Kaiba!

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:34.320
Whatever!  You don't know anything!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:40.560
You don't know why Jonouchi is 
fighting so hard, so stop talking!

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:44.240
That's right!  His sister's eyes are-

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:47.530
Stop!  Don't say anything!

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:54.160
Even the weakest duelist 
has a reason to duel.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:58.880
What's important is whether this burden 
crushes you or whether you keep fighting for it.

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:02.800
Jonouchi, you should regret battling me.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:06.150
You have the eyes of a loser 
who's scared to fight.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:10.640
You'll never be a duelist again.

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:13.150
Kaiba, why are you like this?

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:17.590
Pegasus must be inside that castle.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:22.800
Pegasus J. Crawford is the 
creator of Duel Monsters.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:25.540
His power is limitless.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:32.180
He invented the game rules and all the cards.

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:37.920
On this island, duelists battle for 
Star Chips to reach that castle.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:44.080
But they're nothing more than his pawns.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:51.260
Yugi, even your skills are 
not enough to defeat Pegasus.

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:55.600
I've seen him duel just once before.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:58.820
Actually, I don't know if 
I can even call it a duel.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:04.820
It was the United States King of Duelists 
Championship held at New York Duel Stadium.

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:09.110
I was invited as a guest.

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:14.340
Pegasus's opponent was Keith Howard, the 
top money earner in the United States.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:20.500
Since he walked away with the prize money from 
every tournament, he was known as Bandit Keith.

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:24.720
It's an honor to battle you.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:30.080
When this duel is over, 
I'll be #1 in the world.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.980
Wow!  I wonder who's going to win?

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:38.300
I drew an excellent card.

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:40.880
Are you paying attention?

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:42.900
The game has started.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:46.480
Pegasus kept staring at Keith.

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:54.320
After writing something down, he invited 
a kid sitting behind me to take his seat.

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:58.000
What?  Stop messing around, Pegasus!

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:00.640
I am not messing around.

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:04.430
This boy will duel in my place.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:07.370
Do you think I can win?

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:12.260
No problem.  You will win if 
you follow these instructions.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:16.040
Pegasus!

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.660
Hello, Kaiba boy.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:23.360
By the way, I saw your proposal.

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:28.600
Your Card Battle Simulator 
System is simply wonderful.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:34.260
I'd love Kaiba Corporation and my company 
to work together to make it a reality.

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:37.880
He ran away because he was 
afraid of losing to me.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:41.480
But I don't care as long 
as I get the prize money.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:43.640
I play this card, kid!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.880
Umm...

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:50.000
If you play that card, I should 
play this card in attack position.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:51.360
What?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.550
This stops your Fissure.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:59.940
Impossible!  You know all my strategies?

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:06.190
Oh my god!

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:12.120
Tom wins.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:14.900
I don't know what trick he used.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:21.770
I don't know if that trick would 
work with Duel Disks either.

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:23.770
Pegasus...

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:26.000
I'll play this card.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.750
That card is Koumori Dragon.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:29.480
What?

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:34.050
I predicted that you would play that card.

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:37.540
I've also witnessed his ability.

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:43.920
Kaiba, did you duel Jonouchi to show 
him how difficult dueling can be?

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:48.640
Yugi, I will invade Pegasus's 
castle and defeat Pegasus.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:52.260
I have to get back what I've lost.

00:19:53.660 --> 00:20:00.110
We also have things that we can't 
afford to lose, just like you.

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:05.330
I will defeat Pegasus.

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:11.460
But I will invade Pegasus's 
castle before you.

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:27.220
Welcome, Kaiba boy.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:38.320
After being thoroughly defeated by Kaiba, 
Jonouchi is in big trouble again.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:44.160
Former United States champion Bandit Keith 
and his gang kidnap him to an underground dungeon.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:49.600
Keith's minion Ghost Kotsuzuka challenges 
Jonouchi to a duel on the Graveyard field.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:53.120
Hey!  Don't accept that unfair duel!

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:56.880
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Terror!
Call of the Haunted

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:58.820
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:09.570
The flask glistens

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:17.410
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:26.380
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:34.160
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:39.990
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:44.100
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:52.370
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:56.610
Shower of happiness

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:00.740
You are not alone

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:07.460
You're protected by a 
giant ring of friendship
